WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.300
-Our next guest is

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.334
a Grammy-nominated
singer and songwriter

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.634
whose new single, "brrr,"
is out now.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.334
Please welcome to the show,
Kim Petras, everybody!

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:11.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:17.167
♪♪

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:23.634
♪♪

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:28.100
♪♪

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.434
-Welcome to the show, Kim!

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:30.767
Are you well?
-Thank you!

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:32.634
Yeah, I'm so excited to be here.
Thanks for having me.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.434
-I was so excited to see you
on Saturday.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.033
You made your "SNL" debut,

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:38.534
and I think it's always
a little nerve-wracking

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.033
to appear on "SNL"
for the first time.

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:43.734
You had sort of
a higher bar of entry

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:46.067
than anyone I've ever seen,
because you were sort of

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:48.868
hiding under Sam's dress
and then revealed.

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:51.501
-Yeah.
It was a moment, for sure.

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:53.100
I was under there for
a long time.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.133
-Yeah.
-So it was very well-rehearsed.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:59.033
-And I've got to imagine it's
not super cool and breezy.

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.434
-Not at all.
-Yeah.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:02.300
-Nope. It was very hot.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.501
I was, like, sweating.

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.634
And also, Sam was moving a lot,
so I was like --

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.400
I don't know if you guys know
the little Kim dance,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.667
but I was like --

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:10.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:12.400
You know, I was just
trying to, like --

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.434
because I had to hold it,
because otherwise,

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:16.467
I would get these crazy flyaways
and everyone would be like,

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.901
"She had flyaways last time,"
so it was just like, yeah.

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:20.901
I just had to dodge with Sam.

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:22.667
But worth it.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:24.501
-Someone on TikTok predicted it,
but other than that,

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:25.634
it was a surprise.

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:27.534
-Someone predicted you'd
be under the dress?

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:29.667
-Yes, there's a TikTok
that's like,

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:31.334
"Oh, I bet she's
under the dress,"

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.167
and then they all
scream and jump up.

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:34.868
It's good!

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:38.601
-You also got to go to
the afterparty.

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:40.067
Here you are with the
wonderful host of the evening,

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:41.067
Aubrey Plaza.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.367
-Aubrey! I'm such a fan.

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:46.133
-This is a big deal. Madonna!

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:48.100
Now, had you ever met
Madonna before?

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:53.667
-Um, I met her briefly
at Pride years ago,

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:55.601
but not like this.

00:01:55.601 --> 00:01:59.467
We talked and I was, like,
really obliterated drunk

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:01.634
and I was just like,
"You're my queen!"

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.801
And it was the afterparty
and she just showed up.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.100
I'm sure she thinks I'm crazy.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.167
But yeah, I was like,

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:08.467
"You are the blueprint
for everybody

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:09.634
and you need to know this!

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:11.033
And this album means
so much to me

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:12.133
and 'Confessions
on the Dance Floor'

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:13.200
was the best album ever."

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.534
I was just, like, going ham,

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.200
and then she was like,
"You want to take a picture?"

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.234
She was like, "Mm-hmm."

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:20.968
-By the way,
there's nothing better

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:23.000
than when a celebrity
clocks the moment

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.000
and is like, "I'm gonna
ask you to stop talking."

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.901
-Yeah.
-And we're gonna get

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:28.801
the picture that you're gonna
want from this moment, right?

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:30.934
-Yeah, no, totally, because
I wouldn't have gotten one.

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:32.567
I was like, way too scared.
-Is this the moment after?

00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:36.234
-Yes! [ Laughs ]

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:38.300
-She was just like, it felt like

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.834
she was my only friend
when I was a kid.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:42.033
I listened to her music!

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:44.734
It went on for, like,
10 minutes.

00:02:44.734 --> 00:02:46.467
I was crying my makeup off.

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:48.067
-Oh, my God. What a night.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.567
First you're under a dress,
then you meet Madonna.

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:51.767
There's a lot going on.

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:53.200
-It's a Tuesday for me.
-Yeah, there you go.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.434
-Yeah.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:56.400
-I think you and I live
very different lives.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.133
Another difference,

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.334
I've never been nominated
for a Grammy.

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:00.701
You got nominated for
a Grammy this year.

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:03.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:08.100
-What was the moment like
where you got to find out?

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.801
-My team yelled at me
from downstairs

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:12.834
and just, like,
came into my room

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.100
and I was just, like,
getting ready and I was like,

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.400
"What?" and yeah,
they were just like,

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.601
"You're nominated for a Grammy,"

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.667
and we all started
crying and jumping

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:21.133
and doing the things you do,

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.300
so yeah, it's crazy.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.133
I can't believe it.
-Seems like you've had

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:24.467
a lot of good cries recently.

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:25.834
I think it's a very nice sign.

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:27.501
-Yeah, I cry a lot.

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:28.968
-Yeah, that's alright.

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:31.033
I men, if you're crying for
getting nominated for a Grammy,

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:32.467
like, let the tears flow, right?

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:34.167
-Yeah, for sure.
-Yeah.

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:35.634
-Good cries. Good cries.

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:40.634
-You and Sam, you got nominated
for the song that was your duet,

00:03:40.634 --> 00:03:43.200
and you also set sort of a --

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.133
It was a historical precedent
for LGBTQ representation

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:47.934
at the Grammys, so
congratulations on that as well.

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:51.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:53.200
-Thanks, guys.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.534
Yeah, I mean, it's so crazy.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:04:00.968
I feel like gay clubs raised me
and pop music.

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:04.801
No one loves pop music
more than gay clubs,

00:04:04.801 --> 00:04:09.200
and honestly, I owe everything
I have to the gays in Bushwick.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.701
You guys, honestly, I used to

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:16.200
perform on tables in bars
and whatever,

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.667
and now I'm nominated
for a Grammy.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.501
It's so crazy,
because those were always

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:22.534
the places where I just, like,
felt like I belonged in there,

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:25.834
where like, pop music
and fun music is celebrated

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:28.400
like it has won
a bunch of Grammys.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:32.834
So it's crazy that Sam and I
kind of did this club song

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:35.701
and it got nominated
for a Grammy.

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:38.534
And it's a very gay song,
so thank you, Grammys.

00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:41.334
I really appreciate it.

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:42.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:46.234
-Sam must be an incredible
person to collaborate with,

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:51.067
but I also a video of you
singing with your dog.

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:53.901
-Yeah.
-Your dog Karl, is that right?

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:56.367
-Karl, "Carl" with a K.
-Okay, Karl with a K.

00:04:56.367 --> 00:05:00.067
And now we have a video of you
singing and Karl joining you.

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:02.000
Did this happen naturally
the first time?

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.934
Did Karl just start singing
along with you?

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:07.167
-Yeah, it kind of
happened right away.

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:10.534
Whenever I warm up,
he sits next to me,

00:05:10.534 --> 00:05:14.367
on the chair next to me
and sings with me,

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.467
and he's really good.

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:18.167
He's getting better,
and I'm --

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:19.334
-But this isn't a --

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:20.467
You didn't go to
the pet store and say,

00:05:20.467 --> 00:05:21.901
"Obviously, I'd love a dog
that could sing."

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:24.067
-No, of course I didn't.
-Okay, okay. Gotcha.

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:26.467
-Yeah, and I have
two other dogs,

00:05:26.467 --> 00:05:30.200
so I was not expecting
such a brilliant voice

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.033
to come out of that guy.

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:35.934
-Do the other dogs kind of
think Karl's a lot?

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:37.167
Are they like, ugh?
-Yeah.

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:39.434
They're like,
"There he goes again.

00:05:39.434 --> 00:05:42.801
All the attention."
They're mad in the corner.

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:44.267
-Let's see the
attention-grabbing

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:45.267
Karl the dog.

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:50.701
-[ Singing scales ]

00:05:50.701 --> 00:05:53.167
-[ Howling in tune ]

00:05:53.167 --> 00:05:54.567
-[ Laughs ] Aww.

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:56.434
-[ Singing scales ]

00:05:56.434 --> 00:05:58.634
-[ Howling ]

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:01.434
[ Laughing ]
-Pretty amazing!

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:02.767
[ Applause ]

00:06:02.767 --> 00:06:06.267
Pretty impressive.
-That's Karl.

00:06:06.267 --> 00:06:07.334
He's a star.

00:06:07.334 --> 00:06:10.567
Stealing my shine.
Stop it, Karl!

00:06:10.567 --> 00:06:12.033
-This is a true story.

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:15.634
You are a huge fan of our other
guest tonight, Hilary Duff.

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:17.434
-Yes.
-What is your history

00:06:17.434 --> 00:06:19.234
with Hilary Duff as a fan?

00:06:19.234 --> 00:06:22.934
-Well, "Metamorphosis"
shaped me as a person.

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:25.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.133
I mean, honestly,
"Lizzie McGuire"

00:06:28.133 --> 00:06:30.901
was like, my life
when I was a kid.

00:06:30.901 --> 00:06:32.334
I'm obsessed with her.

00:06:32.334 --> 00:06:33.567
I'm obsessed with her concerts,

00:06:33.567 --> 00:06:35.767
and I was like,
shrieking and freaking out

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:37.100
when I just met her backstage.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.200
It's been so crazy
meeting all these legends,

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.133
and I just, like,
"Okay, here we go.

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:42.934
Just cry again, freak out,
you know."

00:06:42.934 --> 00:06:45.133
But yeah, she just, like,

00:06:45.133 --> 00:06:47.534
is so iconic,
and her music is so good.

00:06:47.534 --> 00:06:50.000
And she really doesn't get
the credit that she deserves.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.901
You know?
-Let's get her out here

00:06:53.901 --> 00:06:55.801
and fix that.
-Pop star.

00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:58.934
-I'm very happy about this
and I want to thank you

00:06:58.934 --> 00:07:00.133
for sticking around.

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:01.767
You're gonna do your new song,
"Brrr."

00:07:01.767 --> 00:07:04.234
Am I saying that...?
Is that a good...?

00:07:04.234 --> 00:07:06.000
That's alright? I can...?
-Yeah, no. That's good.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:06.934
It's not [Rolling R's] "Brrrrr."

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:08.200
-Okay, good.
-Yeah.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.701
-It's "brr"? Alright, great.
Thank you very much.

00:07:10.701 --> 00:07:12.834
And you've also had
a song called "Icy."

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:16.901
Is this sort of winter theme
something that is true to you?

00:07:16.901 --> 00:07:19.634
-Yeah, I mean, I'm from Germany,
so it's cold there.

00:07:19.634 --> 00:07:23.200
And I just feel like
the whole kind of like,

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:27.968
industrial feel of Germany
just offers itself to ice.

00:07:27.968 --> 00:07:31.000
So all my fans keep making memes
of, like, Elsa twerking,

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.067
and I really appreciate it.
-Alright, great.

00:07:33.067 --> 00:07:35.567
-That's honestly what
I want to give, you know?

00:07:35.567 --> 00:07:37.000
A video of Elsa twerking.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.801
So yeah, they're connected.

00:07:38.801 --> 00:07:42.200
I have an ice block in my show,
so yeah.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.067
More ice songs.
-There you go. More ice songs.

00:07:44.067 --> 00:07:46.901
Well, I think probably you were
thinking about that ice block

00:07:46.901 --> 00:07:48.067
when you were under Sam's dress.

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:50.334
You were like,
could have used that today.

00:07:50.334 --> 00:07:52.300
-I could have really
used that then.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.033
It wasn't there.

00:07:54.033 --> 00:07:55.334
-Your fans have an album
to look forward to.

00:07:55.334 --> 00:07:57.501
Tour as well? Are you gonna go
on the road in 2023?

00:07:57.501 --> 00:08:01.300
-Yes, summer. So excited.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:03.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:03.701 --> 00:08:05.467
Yeah, and it's been awhile.

00:08:05.467 --> 00:08:07.501
It was like, before the pandemic
that I toured last.

00:08:07.501 --> 00:08:09.267
-Oh, well, they'll be very, very
happy to see you.

00:08:09.267 --> 00:08:11.801
-Thank God. Thank God.
-Alright.

00:08:11.801 --> 00:08:13.901
I'm very excited to see you
in a few minutes.

00:08:13.901 --> 00:08:16.133
You guys, that's Kim Petras.
Give it up!

00:08:16.133 --> 00:08:19.701
We'll be right back with
her debut TV performance

00:08:19.701 --> 00:08:21.834
of her new single, "Brrr."

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:23.634
-Brr!
-Brr! [Rolling R's]

